activities.content:
To overload constructors, define multiple constructor declarations inside the same class, each with a different parameter signature.

### Valid Overloading Example:
```java
class Employee {
    String name;
    int id;
    double salary;

    // Constructor 1: Zero arguments (default values)
    Employee() {
        name = "Unassigned";
        id = 0;
        salary = 30000.0;
    }

    // Constructor 2: Name and ID only
    Employee(String empName, int empId) {
        name = empName;
        id = empId;
        salary = 30000.0; // Default salary
    }

    // Constructor 3: Full custom data
    Employee(String empName, int empId, double empSalary) {
        name = empName;
        id = empId;
        salary = empSalary;
    }
}
```

### How Java Selects the Constructor:
```java
Employee e1 = new Employee();                      // Calls Constructor 1
Employee e2 = new Employee("Aditi", 101);          // Calls Constructor 2
Employee e3 = new Employee("Rohan", 102, 65000.0); // Calls Constructor 3
```

### What Is NOT Allowed:
Changing only parameter variable names is NOT valid overloading:
```java
// ❌ COMPILE ERROR: Duplicate method Employee(String)!
Employee(String empName) { ... }
Employee(String studentName) { ... }
```
Java differentiates by parameter **data types**, NOT parameter variable names!

activities.codeSnippet:
class Laptop {
    String brand;
    int ramGB;
    double price;

    // Overload 1: Default budget configuration
    Laptop() {
        brand = "Standard";
        ramGB = 8;
        price = 499.99;
    }

    // Overload 2: Brand specified, standard specs
    Laptop(String lBrand) {
        brand = lBrand;
        ramGB = 8;
        price = 599.99;
    }

    // Overload 3: Full custom build
    Laptop(String lBrand, int lRam, double lPrice) {
        brand = lBrand;
        ramGB = lRam;
        price = lPrice;
    }

    void printSpecs() {
        System.out.println(brand + " Laptop | " + ramGB + "GB RAM | $" + price);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Laptop l1 = new Laptop();
        Laptop l2 = new Laptop("Dell");
        Laptop l3 = new Laptop("Apple", 16, 1299.00);

        l1.printSpecs();
        l2.printSpecs();
        l3.printSpecs();
    }
}

class CoffeeOrder {
    String size;
    String milkType;
    int sugarSpoons;

    // 1. Regular Black Coffee
    CoffeeOrder(String s) {
        size = s;
        milkType = "None";
        sugarSpoons = 0;
    }

    // 2. Coffee with custom milk
    CoffeeOrder(String s, String milk) {
        size = s;
        milkType = milk;
        sugarSpoons = 0;
    }

    // 3. Full Custom Coffee
    CoffeeOrder(String s, String milk, int sugar) {
        size = s;
        milkType = milk;
        sugarSpoons = sugar;
    }

    void printSummary() {
        System.out.println(size + " Coffee with " + milkType + " milk and " + sugarSpoons + " sugars");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CoffeeOrder c1 = new CoffeeOrder("Medium");
        CoffeeOrder c2 = new CoffeeOrder("Large", "Oat");
        CoffeeOrder c3 = new CoffeeOrder("Small", "Almond", 2);

        c1.printSummary();
        c2.printSummary();
        c3.printSummary();
    }
}

